1
00:00:00,107 --> 00:00:14,242
(Q31) Tree planting now dominates political and popular agendas and is often presented as an easy answer to the climate crisis, as well as a way for business corporations to offset their carbon emissions.

2
00:00:14,242 --> 00:00:20,137
But unfortunately, tree planting isn’t as straightforward as some people think.

3
00:00:20,137 --> 00:00:30,887
When the wrong trees are planted in the wrong place, it can do considerably more damage than good, failing to help either people or the environment.

4
00:00:30,887 --> 00:00:40,885
Reforestation projects are currently being undertaken on a huge scale in many countries and it’s crucial that the right trees are selected.

5
00:00:40,885 --> 00:00:54,963
A mix of species should always be planted, typical of the local natural forest ecosystem and including rare and endangered species in order to create a rich ecosystem.

6
00:00:54,963 --> 00:01:00,456
It’s important to avoid non-native species that could become invasive.

7
00:01:00,456 --> 00:01:14,880
[Q31答案句] Invasive species are a significant contributor to the current global biodiversity crisis and are often in competition with native species and may threaten their long-term survival.

8
00:01:14,880 --> 00:01:28,596
(Q32) Restoring biodiversity that will maximise carbon capture is key when reforesting an area, but ideally any reforestation project should have several goals.

9
00:01:28,596 --> 00:01:41,705
[Q32答案句] These could include selecting trees that can contribute to wildlife conservation, improve the availability of food for the local community and maintain the stability of soil systems.

10
00:01:41,705 --> 00:01:57,055
(Q33) Meeting as many of these goals as possible, whilst doing no harm to local communities, native ecosystems and vulnerable species, is the sign of a highly successful tree-planting scheme.

11
00:01:57,055 --> 00:02:15,226
To ensure the survival and resilience of a planted forest, it’s vital to use tree seeds with appropriate levels of genetic diversity: the amount of genetic variation found within a species essential for their survival.

12
00:02:15,226 --> 00:02:30,384
[Q33答案句] Using seeds with low genetic diversity generally lowers the resilience of restored forests, which can make them vulnerable to disease and unable to adapt to climate change.

13
00:02:30,384 --> 00:02:38,820
(Q34) Choosing the right location for reforestation projects is as important as choosing the right trees.

14
00:02:38,820 --> 00:02:48,299
Ultimately, the best area for planting trees would be in formerly forested areas that are in poor condition.

15
00:02:48,299 --> 00:03:02,923
It’s better to avoid non-forested landscapes such as natural grasslands, savannas or wetlands as these ecosystems already contribute greatly to capturing carbon.

16
00:03:02,923 --> 00:03:12,308
It would also be advantageous to choose an area where trees could provide other benefits, such as recreational spaces.

17
00:03:12,308 --> 00:03:28,018
[Q34答案句] Reforesting areas which are currently exploited for agriculture should be avoided as this often leads to other areas being deforested.

18
00:03:28,018 --> 00:03:33,968
(Q35) Large-scale reforestation projects require careful planning.

19
00:03:33,968 --> 00:03:41,259
Making the right decisions about where to plant trees depends on having the right information.

20
00:03:41,259 --> 00:03:51,182
[Q35答案句] Having detailed and up-to-date maps identifying high-priority areas for intervention is essential.

21
00:03:51,182 --> 00:04:01,271
(Q36) Drone technology is a useful tool in helping to prioritise and monitor areas of degraded forest for restoration.

22
00:04:01,271 --> 00:04:16,672
[Q36答案句] In Brazil, it’s being used to identify and quantify how parts of the Amazon are being devastated by human activities such as rearing cattle and illegal logging.

23
00:04:16,672 --> 00:04:26,638
(Q37) A good example of where the right trees were picked to achieve a restored forest is in NLampang Province in Northern Thailand.

24
00:04:26,638 --> 00:04:38,671
A previously forested site which had been degraded through mining was reforested by a cement company together with Chiang Mai University.

25
00:04:38,671 --> 00:04:50,945
After spreading 60 cm of topsoil, they planted 14 different native tree species which included several species of fig.

26
00:04:50,945 --> 00:04:59,771
Figs are a keystone species because of the critical role they play in maintaining wildlife populations.

27
00:04:59,771 --> 00:05:14,736
[Q37答案句] They are central to tropical reforestation projects as they accelerate the speed of the recovery process by attracting animals and birds which act as natural seed dispersers.

28
00:05:14,736 --> 00:05:22,563
(Q38) This helps to promote diversity through the healthy regrowth of a wide range of plant species.

29
00:05:22,563 --> 00:05:33,343
Unlike the majority of fruit trees, figs bear fruit all year round, providing a reliable food source for many species.

30
00:05:33,343 --> 00:05:46,304
[Q38答案句] At this site, for example, after only three rainy seasons, monkeys started visiting to eat the fig fruits, naturally dispersing seeds through defecation.

31
00:05:46,304 --> 00:05:56,839
(Q39) Reforestation projects should always aim to make sure that local communities are consulted and involved in the decision-making process.

32
00:05:56,839 --> 00:06:08,183
The restoration of mangrove forests in Madagascar is an example of a project which has succeeded in creating real benefits for the community.

33
00:06:08,183 --> 00:06:25,265
[Q39答案句] Destruction of the mangrove forests had a terrible impact on plant and animal life, and also badly affected the fishing industry, which was a major source of employment for local people living in coastal areas.

34
00:06:25,265 --> 00:06:34,405
(Q40) The reforestation project involved hiring local people to plant and care for the new mangrove trees.

35
00:06:34,405 --> 00:06:43,593
Millions of mangrove trees have now been planted which has resulted in the return of a healthy aquatic ecosystem.

36
00:06:43,593 --> 00:06:51,789
[Q40答案句] The mangroves also act as a defence against the increased threat of flooding caused by climate change.

37
00:06:51,789 --> 00:07:02,310
What’s more, the local economy is more stable and thousands more Madagascans are now able to send their children to school.

38
00:07:02,310 --> 00:07:04,810
One other important point to consider . . .

